course: dictionary
lesson: 14046
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. You can tell which meaning is right by reading the words around it, which is its context. «The monk copied the old manuscript by hand.» The clues are old and by hand, so here a manuscript is a book written by hand.
explain: «The author sent her manuscript to the publisher.» Now the clues are author and publisher. A manuscript here is the writer's own copy before it is printed, not an old book.
explain: «She wrote her notes on manuscript paper.» Manuscript paper has lines for music, so here the word means music written out by hand. Try each meaning in the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found the right one.
fact: A manuscript is a book, story or piece of writing written by hand.
fact: Old manuscripts, from before printing, were copied out by hand, often by monks.
fact: An illuminated manuscript is an old book decorated with gold and colours.
fact: A manuscript can also be the writer's own copy of a book before it is printed, often typed now.
fact: Music written out by hand is also called manuscript, as in manuscript paper.
exercise: «The monk copied the old manuscript by hand.» In this sentence, what is a manuscript? | A type of paper for drawing | A machine that prints books | *A book or piece of writing written by hand, from long ago | A small gold coin
exercise: «The author sent her manuscript to the publisher.» What does manuscript mean here? | A machine for printing | Music written out by hand | An old book decorated with gold | *The writer's own copy of a book before it is printed
exercise: Which kind of writing is manuscript paper for? | Painting pictures | Printing maps | *Writing music by hand | Writing letters to friends
test: Which phrase means an old book decorated with gold and colours? | original manuscript | *illuminated manuscript | manuscript paper | publisher
test: «The original manuscript was lost in the post.» Here, original means | Copied | *The very first one | Typed | Printed
exam: Lily says a manuscript is always an old book. Is she right? | Yes, it always means an old book | Not sure, it has no meaning | No, it always means a printed book with a cover | *No, it can also mean a writer's unprinted copy, or music written by hand
